// FS25 terrain material pass (0x1EB3A314) - draws nearly all ground. Too large/slow to decompile, so this is the
// game's own DXIL with a small patch, reassembled and validated (tools/fs25-decompiler/dxil-patch on fs25-tools:
// patch_ground.py + splice_puddle.py + puddle.hlsl):
//   - adds the RenoDX injection cbuffer (b13, space50)
//   - Wet Ground: roughness = lerp(r, min(r, 0.08), saturate(wet) * CUSTOM_WET_GROUND * 0.75), wet = the game's own
//     wetness (cWetness x rain occlusion). Capped at 75%: beyond that the game's SSR turns grainy on gravel.
//   - Puddles (CUSTOM_PUDDLES = coverage): value-noise puddles placed with the game's terrain uv (TEXCOORD3 - seamless
//     across terrain patches). Flat ground only (shading normal y 0.88-0.96). Wetness drives puddle size; strength
//     fixed. Puddle pixels take the game's env-probe (baked sky) reflection path instead of SSR - the game's SSR
//     shimmered / broke into shards on puddles at any roughness (half-res, stochastic, displaced ground).
// Everything else is the game's own code.
